> And fourthly, I had a pet go hostile on me once after I "bumped"
> him out of a pit.  Is that because I hurt him?  Can they go hostile
> if you "displace" them too much?

Yes to the former; try to #untrap the pet instead. WRT displacement
of pets I never observed any disadvantage. (Another thing is bumping
into your pet while you're stunned or confused, which is a bad move.)

> And on a side note:  how do you "unstack" items?  I really didn't
> want to drop all 12 tripe rations at once.

There's the possibility of counted commands; depending on whether you
have the number pad on or not it's either (e.g.) prefixed by a number
or by the letter <n> followed by a number. It's also possible with
some commands to infix the number, like d5t (to drop five objects of
the object stack in inventory letter t). (Not sure whether that also
depends on the menustyle settings.)

Another application is using the 'name' command to individually name
items of a stack in the inventory list; to do that you have to pick
them up one by one (with the method above).

